From: Amon Koike <amon.koike@daemons.jp>
Subject: [PATCH] build: make key-writer adapters mutually exclusive

Upstream selects the WireGuard netlink key-writer with

    //go:build wireguard_netlink || !wireguard_mikrotik

The trailing `!wireguard_mikrotik` makes netlink the default, which is
correct today because MikroTik is the only other tag. But it means the
file is also compiled in for *any* future adapter tag, so adding a third
key-writer produces a duplicate definition of getKeyWriterService rather
than replacing it.

Narrow the default so each adapter tag deselects it explicitly. This is a
no-op for existing builds:

    (no tags)                  -> netlink       (unchanged)
    -tags wireguard_netlink    -> netlink       (unchanged)
    -tags wireguard_mikrotik   -> mikrotik      (unchanged)
    -tags strongswan_vici      -> vici          (new; previously a
                                                 duplicate-symbol build
                                                 failure)

Applied by this repository's strongSwan image build; carried here so the
change is reviewable in isolation before it is proposed upstream.
---
 wireguardnetlink.go | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/wireguardnetlink.go b/wireguardnetlink.go
index 1111111..2222222 100644
--- a/wireguardnetlink.go
+++ b/wireguardnetlink.go
@@ -1,4 +1,4 @@
-//go:build wireguard_netlink || !wireguard_mikrotik
+//go:build wireguard_netlink || (!wireguard_mikrotik && !strongswan_vici)

 package main

